WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:02.869
-Our first guest tonight
is an Emmy-nominated actress

00:00:02.869 --> 00:00:04.937
you know from her work
on "Saturday Night Live"

00:00:04.937 --> 00:00:06.406
and the Hulu series "Shrill."

00:00:06.406 --> 00:00:11.144
"SNL" airs live this week on NBC
with host Will Forte

00:00:11.144 --> 00:00:13.279
and musical guest Maneskin.

00:00:13.279 --> 00:00:14.614
Please welcome back to the show

00:00:14.614 --> 00:00:16.449
our very good friend
Aidy Bryant.

00:00:16.449 --> 00:00:17.650
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:27.660 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:34.901 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:34.901 --> 00:00:37.636
Hello, Aidy.
-Hello!

00:00:37.636 --> 00:00:40.206
Hello.
-So happy to have you here.

00:00:40.206 --> 00:00:43.109
-Oh, gosh, it feels so good
to be on television.

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:44.510
-[ Laughs ]
You are --

00:00:44.510 --> 00:00:47.013
You are the perfect first guest
for me to have

00:00:47.013 --> 00:00:49.081
after my week away
because of COVID.

00:00:49.081 --> 00:00:51.451
I know "SNL" has obviously been
dealing with COVID, as well.

00:00:51.451 --> 00:00:53.486
You guys had
a pretty gnarly week

00:00:53.486 --> 00:00:54.620
leading into the Christmas show.
-Yeah.

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:57.891
Yeah, chill, I would say.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:57.891 --> 00:01:00.260
No, I mean, it's a weird time.
-Yes.

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:01.627
-Wait. Do you think
I'm the perfect guest

00:01:01.627 --> 00:01:03.229
to have back
because it's like family

00:01:03.229 --> 00:01:05.131
where you can, like,
be dirty around me

00:01:05.131 --> 00:01:07.066
and be post-COVID or something?
[ Laughter ]

00:01:07.066 --> 00:01:08.768
-Yeah.
-Cute.

00:01:08.768 --> 00:01:10.203
[ Laughter ]

00:01:10.203 --> 00:01:11.570
Yeah.
-I don't know why --

00:01:11.570 --> 00:01:12.972
What kind of family
do you have, though?

00:01:12.972 --> 00:01:14.941
You're like...
Because I'm like family,

00:01:14.941 --> 00:01:17.210
so you can be dirty around me?
Like, what?

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:18.811
-Well, I guess I mean, like --

00:01:18.811 --> 00:01:20.446
And I say this
with a lot of love.

00:01:20.446 --> 00:01:22.315
Like, if I [bleep] my pants
in front of my family,

00:01:22.315 --> 00:01:24.984
I'm like, whatever.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:24.984 --> 00:01:26.652
Not that
you're gonna do that.

00:01:26.652 --> 00:01:28.687
-Yeah.
-I just mean, you had COVID,

00:01:28.687 --> 00:01:30.990
here I am kind of
kissing you or whatever.

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:32.692
[ Laughter ]

00:01:32.692 --> 00:01:34.193
-Anyway, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:34.193 --> 00:01:36.962
-"SNL" was scare.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:36.962 --> 00:01:39.832
It was kind of scare Halloween
time but at Christmas.

00:01:39.832 --> 00:01:41.267
-It was Christmas --
You had the Halloween show

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:42.902
at Christmas, but it was --
-Yeah, well, I mean, you know,

00:01:42.902 --> 00:01:45.771
Christmas at "SNL" is usually,
like, so fun.

00:01:45.771 --> 00:01:48.641
-Yeah.
-And we used to do Secret Santa,

00:01:48.641 --> 00:01:52.278
but we stopped
because varying levels

00:01:52.278 --> 00:01:55.281
of caring about it
was making it really sad.

00:01:55.281 --> 00:01:56.449
-Yeah.
-You know?

00:01:56.449 --> 00:01:58.751
-Well, now, I was never --
-It was kind of

00:01:58.751 --> 00:02:01.387
right as you left,
Secret Santa went "Whoo!"

00:02:01.387 --> 00:02:02.789
-Okay.

00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:05.758
I'm so glad because I would
never have stood for that.

00:02:05.758 --> 00:02:09.061
-No, it's so bad.
Because also, you immediately

00:02:09.061 --> 00:02:11.597
are starting to be like,
"Ugh, I got a bad person."

00:02:11.597 --> 00:02:12.765
You know?
And you're like,

00:02:12.765 --> 00:02:16.235
"Oh, this is not the spirit."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:16.235 --> 00:02:18.537
So then,
we stopped Secret Santa,

00:02:18.537 --> 00:02:21.407
and started doing this thing
called the Garbage Party,

00:02:21.407 --> 00:02:24.176
which is, like, kind of
a low-pressure potluck.

00:02:24.176 --> 00:02:25.645
[ Laughter ]
Where it's like,

00:02:25.645 --> 00:02:30.216
bring a bag of chips, bring 30
McDonald's fries, party hats.

00:02:30.216 --> 00:02:33.652
One time, someone brought
jello shots and a dog.

00:02:33.652 --> 00:02:35.455
You know, like --
-A garbage party.

00:02:35.455 --> 00:02:37.423
-Yeah, garbage party.
-Where is a garbage party held?

00:02:37.423 --> 00:02:38.991
-In the writers room.
-In the writers room.

00:02:38.991 --> 00:02:40.860
-On Wednesday after table.
-That's great.

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:43.496
-And it's so fun, and we
didn't get to do it in 2020,

00:02:43.496 --> 00:02:46.465
and so it was, like, "Okay.
This year we're gonna do ano--

00:02:46.465 --> 00:02:49.168
Garbage Party is back, baby."

00:02:49.168 --> 00:02:50.736
I was sending e-mails
being like,

00:02:50.736 --> 00:02:55.474
"This is the biggest one yet.
Everybody get ready to rock."

00:02:55.474 --> 00:02:59.479
So cocky.
I went hard, okay?

00:02:59.479 --> 00:03:03.416
Of course, Monday,
nobody talking about omicron.

00:03:03.416 --> 00:03:06.886
Tuesday, hmm, hearing about it.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:06.886 --> 00:03:11.023
-Wednesday, babe,
your party's cancelled, okay?

00:03:11.023 --> 00:03:13.693
And so I had to send out
an e-mail saying

00:03:13.693 --> 00:03:15.594
the Garbage Party's
back in the grave.

00:03:15.594 --> 00:03:17.496
-Right.
-No party.

00:03:17.496 --> 00:03:23.369
But I had ordered 30 massive
smiley-face balloons...

00:03:23.369 --> 00:03:24.871
[ Laughter ]

00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:27.707
from a place called
the Balloon Saloon downtown.

00:03:27.707 --> 00:03:30.242
-Right, yeah.
-And I realized, I was like,

00:03:30.242 --> 00:03:31.577
"Oh, my God.
Well, I can't have

00:03:31.577 --> 00:03:33.946
the 30 smiley-face balloons
delivered to the office

00:03:33.946 --> 00:03:36.649
when everyone is afraid
of a disease that's in the air."

00:03:36.649 --> 00:03:37.950
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:40.586
-So I was like, "I guess
deliver them to my apartment."

00:03:40.586 --> 00:03:43.656
-Uh-huh.
-So nothing's sadder

00:03:43.656 --> 00:03:46.926
than coming home
after a long day of work

00:03:46.926 --> 00:03:49.728
where everybody's
afraid of a virus

00:03:49.728 --> 00:03:52.398
to an apartment
filled with smiling balloons.

00:03:52.398 --> 00:03:55.034
-I think it's even sadder
than you described.

00:03:55.034 --> 00:03:56.635
[ Laughter ]

00:03:56.635 --> 00:04:01.007
I also think --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:01.007 --> 00:04:05.644
-Kinda cool.
-Like, the balloon travel bag

00:04:05.644 --> 00:04:07.380
makes it look like
they're in quarantine.

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:09.715
-Devastating.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:09.715 --> 00:04:11.451
And I think it's worth knowing,

00:04:11.451 --> 00:04:14.053
like, I just
got them out yesterday.

00:04:14.053 --> 00:04:16.121
-Yeah.
-So they were in my apartment

00:04:16.121 --> 00:04:17.857
for a month.
-Wow.

00:04:17.857 --> 00:04:20.059
Well, now that's actually
a pretty good advertisement

00:04:20.059 --> 00:04:21.794
for the Balloon Saloon.
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:21.794 --> 00:04:23.162
I know!
-Yeah, I mean, that's like

00:04:23.162 --> 00:04:24.697
30 days of helium.

00:04:24.697 --> 00:04:27.466
-Well, there were some
that looked a little rough.

00:04:27.466 --> 00:04:28.968
They were kind of
smiling like...

00:04:28.968 --> 00:04:30.303
[ Laughter ]

00:04:30.303 --> 00:04:31.337
You know?

00:04:31.337 --> 00:04:33.439
But, you know, it's all right.

00:04:33.439 --> 00:04:37.977
-You did a cross-country trip.
-Yeah, yeah, my husband and I,

00:04:37.977 --> 00:04:41.613
at the height of the "omi,"
we said, "Okay.

00:04:41.613 --> 00:04:44.216
Let's get in the car
and drive across country."

00:04:44.216 --> 00:04:46.886
And we did,
and it was okay.

00:04:46.886 --> 00:04:48.688
-Uh-huh.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:48.688 --> 00:04:51.089
-Yeah, I mean it was
really nice, actually.

00:04:51.089 --> 00:04:54.260
I will say, though, like,
in New York, I feel very cool.

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:56.628
-Mm-hmm.
-And the second I get

00:04:56.628 --> 00:05:00.800
out of town, I drop into, like,
who I'm naturally born to be,

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:03.302
which is, like,
kind of like a mom in, like,

00:05:03.302 --> 00:05:06.105
a pumpkin vest, you know?
[ Laughter ]

00:05:06.105 --> 00:05:08.707
Like, I'm just like,
"Look at that!

00:05:08.707 --> 00:05:10.810
Well, hey!"
[ Laughter ]

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:12.345
And, literally,
we would be driving,

00:05:12.345 --> 00:05:14.346
and I couldn't stop myself
from just saying

00:05:14.346 --> 00:05:16.282
what I was seeing,
where I was like, "Cows!"

00:05:16.282 --> 00:05:18.117
[ Laughter ]

00:05:18.117 --> 00:05:20.920
"Look at those hay bales!"
[ Laughter ]

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:23.222
And I really got
my ass handed to me

00:05:23.222 --> 00:05:25.190
because, at a certain point,
we'd been in the car

00:05:25.190 --> 00:05:27.126
for like three days, okay?

00:05:27.126 --> 00:05:30.029
Nothing left to talk about.
-Right.

00:05:30.029 --> 00:05:32.498
-We're approaching,
like, an overpass.

00:05:32.498 --> 00:05:34.900
And finally,
something interesting --

00:05:34.900 --> 00:05:38.804
there's, like, a horse
hauling ass across the overpass.

00:05:38.804 --> 00:05:42.441
And it's like a beautiful
"Black Beauty" horse, you know?

00:05:42.441 --> 00:05:45.510
And I'm like,
"Oh! Look at that horse!

00:05:45.510 --> 00:05:47.479
He's running!"
And then we see

00:05:47.479 --> 00:05:50.817
there's a man
behind the horse, chasing.

00:05:50.817 --> 00:05:52.785
[ Laughter ]

00:05:52.785 --> 00:05:54.554
And I'm, like,
"This is the best thing

00:05:54.554 --> 00:05:55.654
that's ever happened to me."

00:05:55.654 --> 00:05:57.389
But then, he's not, like,
bouncing.

00:05:57.389 --> 00:05:59.825
He's gliding.
And I'm like,

00:05:59.825 --> 00:06:02.328
"Oh, my God,
he's on a skateboard."

00:06:02.328 --> 00:06:05.464
Now, I'm saying this
all out loud.

00:06:05.464 --> 00:06:07.833
I'm like,
"Oh! The horse is running!

00:06:07.833 --> 00:06:08.867
He's on a skateboard!

00:06:08.867 --> 00:06:11.337
The man chasing him
is skateboarding!

00:06:11.337 --> 00:06:13.572
No! He's going so fast,

00:06:13.572 --> 00:06:16.909
he must have a rope on the horse
with the skateboard!"

00:06:16.909 --> 00:06:18.411
And then we got a little closer,

00:06:18.411 --> 00:06:20.546
and it was a man
with a horse and buggy.

00:06:20.546 --> 00:06:25.885
[ Laughter ]

00:06:25.885 --> 00:06:29.856
My husband
has been roasting my ass.

00:06:29.856 --> 00:06:31.189
[ Laughter ]

00:06:31.189 --> 00:06:33.559
Everywhere we go, he's like,
"It's on a skateboard."

00:06:33.559 --> 00:06:35.227
[ Laughter ]

00:06:35.227 --> 00:06:37.262
Hell for me.
Hell.

00:06:37.262 --> 00:06:39.098
-It's always -- yeah.

00:06:39.098 --> 00:06:40.599
Yeah, 'cause the thing is,
you've heard --

00:06:40.599 --> 00:06:43.269
when you said horse and buggy,
I immediately thought,

00:06:43.269 --> 00:06:46.104
"I've heard that combo before."
-Sure.

00:06:46.104 --> 00:06:48.240
-Horse and skateboard?
-Horse, rope, and skateboard?

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:50.209
[ Laughter ]
No.

00:06:50.209 --> 00:06:51.477
-"I'll take
the horse and skateboard

00:06:51.477 --> 00:06:54.980
down to the grain store."
[ Laughter ]

00:06:54.980 --> 00:06:57.316
We --
I want to ask you this question.

00:06:57.316 --> 00:07:00.586
Very tragically,
we lost Bob Saget.

00:07:00.586 --> 00:07:02.121
-Yes.
-Who was --

00:07:02.121 --> 00:07:04.623
I was lucky enough to have met
the sweetest guy in the world.

00:07:04.623 --> 00:07:06.458
But you met him
when you were very young.

00:07:06.458 --> 00:07:08.361
-I met him when I was a child,

00:07:08.361 --> 00:07:11.163
and it was
a totally formative experience.

00:07:11.163 --> 00:07:13.198
I mean, I'll just give you,
like, a little context,

00:07:13.198 --> 00:07:16.668
which is,
I grew up in Phoenix, Arizona --

00:07:16.668 --> 00:07:18.904
not exactly
showbiz headquarters.

00:07:18.904 --> 00:07:20.706
Okay?
More lizard headquarters.

00:07:20.706 --> 00:07:22.675
[ Laughter ]

00:07:22.675 --> 00:07:25.644
And so, as a kid,
you know, I loved TV.

00:07:25.644 --> 00:07:27.479
I was obsessed
with "Full House."

00:07:27.479 --> 00:07:29.114
I loved the Olsen twins.

00:07:29.114 --> 00:07:30.482
I just thought it was,
like, so funny.

00:07:30.482 --> 00:07:32.518
I loved the show.
So, I'm, like,

00:07:32.518 --> 00:07:35.053
obsessed with showbiz,
and my closest

00:07:35.053 --> 00:07:37.690
showbiz connection
that I had was,

00:07:37.690 --> 00:07:40.259
my mom's friend
was a nail technician,

00:07:40.259 --> 00:07:43.896
and on the side, he was in
the Phoenix Gay Men's Choir.

00:07:43.896 --> 00:07:46.364
Okay?
So we would go to these shows

00:07:46.364 --> 00:07:49.234
where like 50 gay men
are singing their hearts out,

00:07:49.234 --> 00:07:50.937
and I would be like,
"I should be up there."

00:07:50.937 --> 00:07:52.404
[ Laughter ]

00:07:52.404 --> 00:07:54.941
"I should be up there
singing a solo!"

00:07:54.941 --> 00:07:57.876
But I was, like, obsessed with
him, because he had showbiz.

00:07:57.876 --> 00:07:59.979
-Yeah.
-And then, as a side gig, later,

00:07:59.979 --> 00:08:03.081
he started --
he was the voice of the news.

00:08:03.081 --> 00:08:05.884
So he would be the one who would
go in and record voiceovers,

00:08:05.884 --> 00:08:07.553
being like,
"Tonight at 10:00..."

00:08:07.553 --> 00:08:09.521
-Oh, wow.
That's a big job.

00:08:09.521 --> 00:08:11.390
-So cool -- to me.
-Yeah.

00:08:11.390 --> 00:08:13.626
So, I was like 7,
and he was like,

00:08:13.626 --> 00:08:16.061
"If you want, you could come
watch me record

00:08:16.061 --> 00:08:17.930
the news voiceovers."

00:08:17.930 --> 00:08:20.633
I was like, "Yes, I want that."
[ Laughter ]

00:08:20.633 --> 00:08:23.569
So, I go with him.
We're in the news station,

00:08:23.569 --> 00:08:25.104
we're crossing the newsroom,

00:08:25.104 --> 00:08:28.608
and there is Bob Saget,
from "Full House."

00:08:28.608 --> 00:08:31.410
He's there to promote
his stand-up in Phoenix.

00:08:31.410 --> 00:08:34.780
But I'm like, "He's here
to take me on the show."

00:08:34.780 --> 00:08:37.683
[ Laughter ]

00:08:37.683 --> 00:08:42.187
And I will tell you,
he was so kind to me.

00:08:42.187 --> 00:08:47.192
He took 5, 10 minutes,
chatted with me about TV,

00:08:47.192 --> 00:08:49.996
how it works,
about "Full House."

00:08:49.996 --> 00:08:52.264
You know, I'm like a dummy.

00:08:52.264 --> 00:08:54.734
I think I maybe had like
one tooth, you know?

00:08:54.734 --> 00:08:56.168
[ Laughter ]

00:08:56.168 --> 00:09:00.606
He was so generous and kind
to me, and I always feel so --

00:09:00.606 --> 00:09:02.574
I mean, for years,
I thought about, like,

00:09:02.574 --> 00:09:05.644
my brush with fame,
my brush with celebrity.

00:09:05.644 --> 00:09:09.014
And I'm so grateful
that it was so nice.

00:09:09.014 --> 00:09:10.883
-Yeah.
-Because then, when I wanted

00:09:10.883 --> 00:09:12.852
to get into entertainment,
I was like,

00:09:12.852 --> 00:09:14.653
"Well, that's how nice
everybody is."

00:09:14.653 --> 00:09:16.288
[ Laughter ]

00:09:16.288 --> 00:09:18.691
"They're all like him."

00:09:18.691 --> 00:09:21.360
So, I'm forever grateful
to him for that.

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:22.995
-Ah, that's a lovely story.
Thanks so much for sharing it,

00:09:22.995 --> 00:09:24.096
and thanks for being here.
-Yeah.

00:09:24.096 --> 00:09:25.164
-It's always so great
to see you, Aidy.

00:09:25.164 --> 00:09:27.466
-Come on.
-Aidy Bryant!

00:09:27.466 --> 00:09:31.037
"SNL" airs live this week
with Will Forte.

